Installing Petit-ami

First of all, remember that petit-ami is in development. This means that
everything may not work perfectly.

Getting the source

The project lives on GitHub:

    https://github.com/samiam95124/amitk

Fetch it with git. The tree carries submodules (curses ports of nano,
htop and the BSD games), so clone with them included:

    git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/samiam95124/amitk.git
    cd amitk

If you cloned without the submodules, fill them in with:

    git submodule update --init

To bring an existing tree up to date later:

    git pull
    git submodule update

Building

The configure script installs the packages Ami builds against, with
sudo apt-get -y install on Linux: alsa and its development files,
openssl, fluidsynth, gawk and the rest. It does not ask first, so run it
on a machine where that is welcome. To install them yourself instead,
see the "make sure used packages are installed." section in configure.

Steps to install

Linux:

. setpath
./configure
make

Windows:

setpath
configure
make

BSD and similar systems use gmake in place of make.

setpath puts the tree's bin directory on the path, so what is built there
runs by name. It is the first of the steps for that reason.
